es":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6600 XT (RADV NAVI23) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nNormally, AudioStreamInteractive should wait for a stream to complete or reach the end of its beat count before progressing to the next clip.\n\nIf these clips are replaced with an AudioStreamRandomizer, they'll all play at once, as if they have zero length.\n\nHere's the normal setup:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0032528d-386b-493b-b378-f1fb805469ae)\n\nAnd the setup that causes this issue:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/72b95184-b8e3-4858-b369-77c32fdddf55)\n\nIdeally, these two setups should produce the same result.\n\nOf note: this works as expected with other streams such as AudioStreamPlaylist. Could be related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104684\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1) Create an AudioStreamPlayer\n2) Give it an AudioStreamInteractive\n3) Put at least two audio clips, with the first having \"auto advance\" enabled and set to go to the second clip.\n4) If you put in two wav or ogg streams, it should behave as expected\n5) Replace the clips with AudioStreamRandomizer streams, with the same wav/ogg stream inside it.\n6) Play the stream and all streams will play at once.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mvp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19969265/mvp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","grava